  "description": "<p>migration-utils currently migrates objects as archival groups. This is not necessarily desirable and has two potentially negative consequences:</p>\n\n<p>1. The object is versioned for every change to any of its parts, causing OCFL version inflation<br/>\n2. The entire object is locked whenever any part of it is updated, meaning that two binaries within the same object cannot be updated concurrently</p>\n\n<p>Example object with 121 versions from Jakov M. Vežić:</p>\n\n<p>So the original in Fedora 3 has:<br/>\nRELS-EXT: 48 versions<br/>\nMODS: 18 versions<br/>\nDC: 34 versions<br/>\nFILE0: 4 versions<br/>\nTN: 5 versions<br/>\nSTATUS_INGEST: 7 versions<br/>\nFILE1: 2 versions<br/>\nFULL_TEXT: 1 version</p>\n\n<p>inventory.json is 635K</p>\n\n<p>migration-utils should allow the user to decide how they want their objects modeled.</p>",
